th> as before.</p><p>Scripts <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></math> as before.</p><p>Sum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> as before.</p><p>Tensor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>c</mi><none></none></mmultiscripts></math> as before.</p><p>Bars <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>‖</mo></math> as before.</p><p>Parentheses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi></math> as before.</p><p>Enclosure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"box\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></menclose></math> as before.</p><p>Fraction rules <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> as before.</p><p>The result, when it arrives, is smaller than the build-up suggests, and the author says as much, which is part of why the paper is still read.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <script type=\"math/tex\">\\cancel{x}+\\bcancel{y}+\\xcancel{z}</script> as before.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <script type=\"math/tex\">\\boxed{a^2+b^2=c^2}</script> as before.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <script type=\"math/tex\">\\sout{struck}\\,\\underline{under}\\,\\overline{over}</script> as before.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <script type=\"math/tex